1. Introduction

MRIS Technologies Limited respects your privacy. This Privacy Policy explains how PDF MRIS accesses, processes, and protects information when you use the application.

2. Document Processing

PDF MRIS is designed to process supported PDF and office documents locally on your device.

Your personal documents are not uploaded to our external servers as part of the application's local document processing functionality.

3. File and Storage Access

The application may request access to files and folders that you choose to open, view, edit, organize, or manage.

File access is used solely to provide the requested document-related functionality.

We do not claim ownership of your files or their contents.

4. Information Collection

PDF MRIS is designed to avoid collecting or accessing the contents of your personal documents for our own purposes.

Information that may be processed by the application depends on the features you use and the application's technical implementation.

If future versions introduce analytics, crash reporting, advertising, cloud services, or other third-party integrations, the relevant information practices will be disclosed in an updated Privacy Policy.

5. Data Sharing

We do not sell your personal documents or their contents.

Documents remain under your control. If you choose to share a document through another application or external service, that sharing is subject to the privacy practices of the receiving service.

6. Data Security

We aim to protect information handled by PDF MRIS through appropriate technical and organizational measures.

However, no software application or electronic storage method can guarantee absolute security.

Users should maintain appropriate backups and protect access to their devices.

7. Children's Privacy

PDF MRIS is not designed to knowingly collect personal information from children. If you believe that personal information has been collected inappropriately, please contact us.

8. Policy Updates

We may update this Privacy Policy to reflect changes in application features, applicable laws, or data-handling practices.

Any revised version will include an updated effective date and will be made available through appropriate channels.

